ENTRY 12473 {"id":12473,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"docs/research/phase1-apis.md:202:  interface StartOptions { env?, cwd?, pty?: {cols,rows}, timeoutMs?, signal?: AbortSignal,\ndocs/session-api.md:55:   - `cancel`: `Conversation.abort()`: withdraws queued inputs, aborts the running turn, resolves when idle.\npackages/orchestrator/test/sessions-fail.test.ts:110:  it(\"aborts even though the failure update changed no row, if the session is already failed\", async () => {\npackages/orchestrator/src/host.ts:260:  /** Withdraws queued inputs, aborts the running turn and resolves once the conversation is idle. */\npackages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts:122:   * ones again: `abort` is idempotent and a no-op on an idle conversation.\n  // own connection and holds the ownership lock on it, and neither may share it.\n  const pool = createPool(config.databaseUrl, `${config.instance}-inbox`, 10);\n  const server = createOrchestratorServer({\n    lifecycle,\n    authenticate: tokenAuthenticator(config.apiTokens),\n    pool,\n    control: config.control,\n  });\n  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.listen(config.port, resolve));\n  log(\"listening\", { instance: config.instance, port: config.port });\n\n  const running: { inbox?: InboxLoop; service?: SessionService; sweeper?: OrphanSweeper } = {};\n  const stop = new AbortController();\n  const shutdown = (signal: string): void => {\n    log(\"shutdown\", { signal });\n    stop.abort();\n    server.close();\n    void (async () => {\n      running.service?.stop();\n      running.sweeper?.stop();\n      await running.inbox?.stop();\n      await lifecycle.host?.close();\n      server.closeAllConnections();\n      await pool.end().catch(() => undefined);\n    })().finally(() => process.exit(0));\n    setTimeout(() => process.exit(0), 10_000).unref();\n  };\n  process.on(\"SIGTERM\", () => shutdown(\"SIGTERM\"));\n  process.on(\"SIGINT\", () => shutdown(\"SIGINT\"));\n\n  for (;;) {\n    try {\n      await applyMigrations(pool);\n      break;\n    } catch (error) {\n      log(\"migrate-failed\", { message: errorMessage(error) });\n/** What a run that ended without an answer means for the session (Pi Durable `RunFailure`, plus the text of the error). */\nexport interface RunOutcome {\n  reason: string;\n  detail?: string;\n}\n\n/**\n * Model-side signs that the credentials are not accepted: an HTTP status of 401 or 403 from the provider (a missing\n * or revoked key, a revoked OneCLI grant leaves the gateway injecting nothing), 407 from the gateway itself (the\n * agent token was deleted or regenerated), the gateway's own answer when the agent has no grant for the host (a 401\n * whose JSON body, which is all pi-ai keeps, reads `access_restricted` / `this agent does not have access`), or the\n * usual wording. Status codes must stand alone, so a request id or a\n * byte count that happens to contain 401 does not match.\n */\nconst REJECTED =\n  /(?<![a-z0-9])(?:401|403|407)(?![a-z0-9])|unauthori[sz]ed|forbidden|invalid[ _-]?api[ _-]?key|incorrect api key|proxy authentication|authentication[ _-]?(?:error|failed)|permission[ _-]?denied|access_restricted|does not have access/i;\n\n/**\n * The terminal failure a run outcome maps to, or undefined when the session stays usable.\n *  - A model error that reads as rejected credentials is terminal: nothing in the orchestrator can fix a grant, and\n *    retrying only repeats paid or rate-limited calls. (pi-ai does not retry these statuses either.)\n *  - `turn_limit` is the per-session turn budget (`maxTurns`).\n *  - Everything else (a 429 that outlasted the retries, a network error, an abort) leaves the session active: the\n *    next message starts a new run.\n */\nexport function terminalFailure(outcome: RunOutcome): string | undefined {\n  if (outcome.reason === \"turn_limit\") {\n    return \"turn budget exhausted: the session used all the model turns it is allowed\";\n  }\n  if (outcome.reason === \"model_error\" && REJECTED.test(outcome.detail ?? \"\")) {\n    return \"model credentials were rejected (401/403): the OneCLI agent token or its grant for this provider is missing or revoked\";\n  }\n  return undefined;\n}\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 12487 {"id":12487,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"[thinking]## Findings\n\n### 1. One stalled submission blocks all run watches\n\n- Severity: medium\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/orchestrator/src/watcher.ts:61\n- What happens: Lookups and failure handlers run sequentially under a single polling guard. If one lookup or handler stalls, later submissions are never checked, and subsequent timer ticks cannot start another pass. For example, a handler waiting for its conversation to become idle can prevent an unrelated session’s terminal model failure from being detected.\n- Evidence: `await this.#options.lookup(...)` and `await this.#options.onUnanswered(...)` execute inside the loop; `if (this.#polling) return` rejects overlapping polls.\n- Fix idea: Process watches independently with bounded concurrency, and apply timeouts or cancellation so a stalled operation cannot block unrelated submissions.\n\nEND-OF-REPORT"}]}
DONE
